# SECTION 26 — Scenario-Based Interview Questions (3–5 Years)

These evaluate practical engineering judgment rather than API knowledge.

* A component re-renders 500 times. How do you debug it?
* Your app becomes slow after adding Redux. What would you investigate?
* A list of 50,000 items freezes the UI. How would you optimize it?
* API requests are firing twice in development. Why?
* How would you implement optimistic updates?
* How would you prevent duplicate API calls?
* How would you cancel an in-flight request when a component unmounts?
* How would you implement role-based access control (RBAC)?
* How would you design a reusable data table?
* How would you implement dark mode across an application?
* How would you share state between unrelated components?
* How would you implement offline support?
* How would you optimize a dashboard with multiple charts?
* How would you manage forms with 100+ fields?
* How would you migrate a large React application incrementally?
* How would you handle feature flags?
* How would you structure a monorepo with shared UI components?
* How would you debug a memory leak in React?
* How would you ensure accessibility in a complex form?
* How would you profile and reduce bundle size?

