## Suggested Study Order (Priority)

1. JavaScript Fundamentals
2. Browser Internals
3. React Fundamentals
4. Hooks (especially `useEffect`)
5. Rendering & React Fiber
6. Performance Optimization
7. State Management (Redux Toolkit, Context, React Query)
8. Routing & API Integration
9. Forms & Validation
10. TypeScript with React
11. Testing
12. Accessibility
13. Security
14. Project Architecture
15. Frontend System Design
16. Real-world coding exercises
17. Scenario-based interview practice

Covering these sections thoroughly will prepare you for the vast majority of React.js frontend interviews in the **3–5 years** experience range, including product companies, startups, and large enterprise organizations.
